# Python + JupyterLab + VS Code + LLM Setup — Student Training Plan

**Audience:** Students new to Python, Jupyter, and AI/LLM tooling
**Platforms covered:** Windows and macOS
**Estimated time:** 2–3 hours (can be split across two sessions)

## Learning Objectives

By the end of this training, students will be able to:

1. Install Anaconda and create isolated Python environments with conda
2. Install and use JupyterLab / Jupyter Notebook
3. Install and configure VS Code as an alternative Python/Jupyter editor
4. Verify their environment with core data libraries (pandas, numpy, matplotlib)
5. Install and run a local LLM with Ollama
6. Install the OpenAI SDK and make a first API call

## Prerequisites

- A laptop (Windows 10/11 or macOS 12+) with admin rights to install software
- At least 10 GB free disk space
- Stable internet connection
- (For Module 9–10) A free [Ollama](https://ollama.com) download and, optionally, an [OpenAI API key](https://platform.openai.com/api-keys)

